sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-blinded-sample-audit-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Morphometric validation: 56/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Computes rasterised silhouette morphometrics (ap_length, ml_width, aspect, area, head/tail/eye/pharynx counts, and rel_wt_length) in morphometrics(), verifies wild-type dimensions against the database radii (557.6 x 119.8 vs 560 x 120 Planform units), and exports a full table via write_csv(). Held below 60 because no quantitative IoU or landmark comparison against real planarian photographs or published software screenshots is performed inside the script at commit 5659d5e. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L418–L444: morphometrics() computes AP length, ML width, aspect ratio, area, and organ counts <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L418-L444>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L716–L731: write_csv() exports per-morphology morphometrics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5659d5e/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L716-L731>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): wild-type silhouette AP length = 557.6 Planform units (reference 560, PlanformDB 2.5.0 RegionParam/RegionsLink of morphology 1 (80+200+200+80)) [union of decoded region outlines of Morphology 1, rasterised; bbox extent along the AP axis]; wild-type silhouette ML width = 119.8 Planform units (reference 120, trunk lateral radii 60+60) [as above, across the ML axis]; wild-type AP/ML aspect = 4.653 ratio (reference 4.667, encoded radii) [AP length / ML width of the decoded silhouette] — S. mediterranea in Lobo et al. 2013 Fig. 1A is of this order; the formalism, not a specimen, is the reference; morphologies rendered = 369 count [Morphology rows with at least one encoded region] — 372 rows in the database; 3 have no regions (Lethal, Midbody Buldge, Double head, side tail); distinct body silhouettes = 167 count (reference 369, upper bound: one silhouette per morphology) [unique (AP length, ML width, area to 100 units, #heads, #tails) tuples over all rendered morphologies] — 115 morphologies share the wild-type body and differ only in organs (ectopic eyes, doubled CNS, pharynx position, ...), which is how the database encodes them; distinct encodings (regions + links + organs) = 369 count (reference 369, every morphology row is a distinct phenotype) [unique tuples of every encoded number read from the database]; IoU wild type vs double head (#24) = 0.8884 ratio (reference < 1; the two bodies differ only at the posterior cap (tail -> second head), the rest of the difference is organs) [intersection-over-union of the two decoded silhouettes on a shared canvas (region centres aligned by layout)]; IoU wild type vs headless (#20) = 0.6116 ratio (reference ≈ (trunk+tail area)/(whole-body area) if the head is simply absent) [as above]." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.56"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation (2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphometric validation' for Planaria (Schmidtea mediterranea, Dugesia japonica)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

